    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "will is just a variable that burns out. i've used it up. i've tried the \"force of will\" thing for years and it only results in more friction and more heat, which just leads back to more entropy. i'm looking at the math of it all, and the energy cost of continuing to exist just to fight an inevitable decay is becoming harder to justify. it feels like i'm just prolonging the heat death of my own life by staying in the equation. isn't there a certain kind of peace in just accepting that some things are meant to end? that the collapse is the natural state?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
